        "original_id": "3e0610a0-e15e-5806-92dc-d8af189461d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeanie Buss, Jerry Buss\n- Organizations: Los Angeles Lakers, National Basketball Association\n- Roles: real estate investor, businessman, investor, chemist, philanthropist, majority owner\n- Concepts: Showtime era, league championships\n\nFacts:\n- Jerry Buss was born on January 27, 1933, and died on February 18, 2013.\n- Jerry Buss was an American businessman, investor, chemist, and philanthropist.\n- Jerry Buss was a real estate investor who later owned the Los Angeles Lakers and other sports businesses.\n- Jerry Buss was the majority owner of the Los Angeles Lakers in the National Basketball Association.\n- The Los Angeles Lakers won 10 league championships under Jerry Buss's ownership.\n- The Los Angeles Lakers' championship success under Jerry Buss was highlighted by the team's Showtime era during the 1980s.\n- Jeanie Buss is a daughter of Jerry Buss.",
